          "path": "_m/q/s/1/5/naval-communication-station-harold-e-holt-wp/naval-communication-st.jpg",
          "filename": "Harold E Holt Naval Base.jpg",
          "caption": "Naval Communication Station Harold E. Holt near Exmouth, Western Australia.  The radio masts are part of a large wire antenna which is used to transmit very low frequency (VLF) radio waves to communicate with submerged submarines.  This type of antenna is known as a \"Goliath\", a type of umbrella antenna, but has been heavily modified.  It consists of a ring of steel masts which support a network of horizontal cables radiating from the central mast.  The central mast acts as the radiating element, while the horizontal cables serve as a capacitive top-load, creating a large capacitor with the ground.  This serves to increase the current in the central radiator, increasing the radiated power.",
          "alt": "Naval Communication Station Harold E. Holt near Exmouth, Western Australia.  The radio masts are part of a large wire antenna which is used to transmit very low frequency (VLF) radio waves to communicate with submerged submarines.  This type of antenna is known as a \"Goliath\", a type of umbrella antenna, but has been heavily modified.  It consists of a ring of steel masts which support a network of horizontal cables radiating from the central mast.  The central mast acts as the radiating element, while the horizontal cables serve as a capacitive top-load, creating a large capacitor with the ground.  This serves to increase the current in the central radiator, increasing the radiated power.",
          "width": 1280,
